The medieval forests of Mara and Mondrem were noted for having **red deer**, **fallow deer** (and also roe deer).  Other parts of the world that are known to have the same species are:

* **Fallow deer (Dama dama)** – besides medieval Cheshire, fallow deer now occur in many places where they have been introduced, for example:  
  * the Caribbean islands of **Antigua & Barbuda**;  
  * **Argentina**, **South Africa**, the islands of **Fernando Pó, São Tomé, Madagascar, Mauritius, Mayotte, Réunion, Seychelles, Comoro Islands**;  
  * North‑African countries **Morocco, Algeria, Tunisia**;  
  * Mediterranean islands **Cyprus, Israel, Cape Verde, Lebanon**;  
  * **Australia**, **New Zealand**, **Canada**, the **United States**, the **Falkland Islands** and **Peru
